.codex-trust-modal
    .modal-header
        .header-main
            .warning-mark
                i.fas.fa-shield-halved
            .heading
                h5.modal-title(translate) Codex runs with hook trust disabled
                .modal-subtitle(translate) Required for session monitoring
        button.close-button(
            type='button',
            (click)='acknowledge()',
            [attr.aria-label]='"Close" | translate',
        ) ×

    .modal-body
        p.lead(translate)
            | Monitoring only works if Codex runs the hooks vibby installs, so vibby
            | starts it with #[code --dangerously-bypass-hook-trust].
        .impact
            .impact-row
                i.fas.fa-circle-exclamation
                span(translate) Codex also stops reviewing every other hook it loads, including hooks from plugins and from cloud or MDM policy.
            .impact-row
                i.fas.fa-circle-exclamation
                span(translate) Hooks can run outside the Codex sandbox.
        p.escape-hatch(translate)
            | Turn Codex off under Settings → AI to stop launching it this way.

    .modal-footer
        button.btn.btn-primary(type='button', (click)='acknowledge()', autofocus, translate) Got it
